---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { routeUrl } from '../../i18n';

const lang = 'en' as const;
const lastUpdated = 'June 22, 2026';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy · Accanto"
  description="How Accanto handles your personal data: minimum collection, no profiling, full export, self-hosting option."
>
  <article class="container-page container-prose">
    <p class="eyebrow mb-3">Privacy</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold mb-4">Privacy summary</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-accanto-500 mb-6">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <aside class="rounded-lg border border-accanto-200 bg-accanto-50 p-4 mb-8 text-sm">
      The authoritative, GDPR-compliant version of this notice is published in Italian at
      <a href="/it/privacy" class="underline font-semibold">/it/privacy</a>. The English summary below
      mirrors its key points; in case of conflicting interpretations, the Italian text prevails.
    </aside>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Account data: email, hashed password, display name, language preference, optional 2FA.</li>
      <li>Your content: notes, timeline, symptoms, doctor questions, uploaded documents, members of
      your "care circles". May include health-related data of the person you assist (special
      category under art. 9 GDPR).</li>
      <li>Technical data: IP address, user-agent, session timestamps, audit logs.</li>
      <li>Push tokens (only when notifications are explicitly enabled).</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What we don't do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We don't sell your data.</li>
      <li>We don't run advertising profiling.</li>
      <li>We don't embed third-party analytics or trackers.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Controller</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>PRESTIA.DEV S.A.S. DI PRESTIA ANDREA</strong> — Viale Bruno Rizzieri 199C, 00173 Rome
      (RM), Italy. VAT IT17486541000. REA RM-1721153.<br />
      Privacy contact: <a href="mailto:support@accanto.care">support@accanto.care</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>You can exercise the rights granted by GDPR (access, rectification, erasure, restriction,
    portability, objection, consent withdrawal) at any time. Most of them are available directly
    inside the Account section of the app. For specific requests email
    <a href="mailto:support@accanto.care">support@accanto.care</a>. You may also file a complaint
    with the Italian Data Protection Authority
    (<a href="https://www.garanteprivacy.it" target="_blank" rel="noopener">garanteprivacy.it</a>).</p>

    <h2>Sub-processors</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>IONOS Cloud (Germany, EU) — hosting and database.</li>
      <li>Expo / 650 Industries (US) — push notification delivery.</li>
      <li>Apple APNs (US), Google FCM (US) — push delivery on iOS/Android.</li>
      <li>App Store and Play Store — app distribution.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Transfers outside the EU rely on the EU–U.S. Data Privacy Framework or Standard Contractual
    Clauses.</p>

    <h2>Medical disclaimer</h2>
    <p>Accanto is <strong>not a medical device</strong> within the meaning of Regulation (EU) 2017/745
    and does not replace professional medical advice. In case of emergency call 112 (EU) or your
    local emergency number.</p>

    <p class="text-sm text-accanto-500 mt-10">
      For any privacy-related question contact <a href="mailto:support@accanto.care">support@accanto.care</a>
      or visit our <a href={routeUrl('contact', lang)}>Contact</a> page.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
